// Accounting write, phase 3a (1 Nov 2026): the Sales tab of the QuickBooks Online and Xero
// connection — app/settings/AccountingSalesPanel.tsx — where the owner previews and approves the
// invoices, payments and refunds NivaDesk sends to the books. Every reason code the server gives
// (functions/accountingPosting.js, accounting/posting/documents.js and events.js) is here in words.
// Merged in language.ts with mergeMissingIntoTranslations: a key another screen already
// translates ("Refresh", "Sent", "Invoice"…) keeps that translation. NivaDesk, QuickBooks, Xero,
// Stripe, PayPal, Pro and Team stay as they are in every language, and so do the {provider} /
// {count} / {code} / {account} / {method} / {orders} / {date} / {created} / {refreshed} /
// {changed} placeholders, filled in after translation. Xero's own setting "Enable payments to
// this account" is quoted in English, as Xero shows it.
